@startuml SAYCEP_UseCase
' SAYCEP - Use Case Diagram (Assignment 2, Q4.1)
' Names here are authoritative across all four diagrams and the requirements.
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Enrolled Student" as Student
actor "School-Leaver" as Leaver
actor "Youth User" as User
actor "Data Administrator" as Admin
actor "O*NET Dataset" as ONET

Student --|> User
Leaver --|> User

rectangle "SAYCEP System Boundary" {
  usecase "UC-01 Create Profile" as UC1
  usecase "UC-02 Capture Skill Profile" as UC2
  usecase "UC-03 Select Target Occupation" as UC3
  usecase "UC-04 Search Occupation Catalogue" as UC4
  usecase "UC-05 Browse by Preparation Level" as UC5
  usecase "UC-06 Recommend Occupations" as UC6
  usecase "UC-07 Analyse Skills Gap" as UC7
  usecase "UC-08 Generate Career Pathway" as UC8
  usecase "UC-09 View Data Provenance" as UC9
  usecase "UC-10 Load Occupation Data" as UC10
}

User --> UC1
User --> UC7
User --> UC8
Student --> UC4
Leaver --> UC5
Admin --> UC10

UC1 ..> UC2 : <<include>>
UC4 ..> UC3 : <<include>>
UC5 ..> UC3 : <<include>>
UC5 ..> UC6 : <<include>>
UC7 ..> UC2 : <<include>>
UC7 ..> UC3 : <<include>>
UC8 ..> UC7 : <<include>>
UC9 ..> UC7 : <<extend>>
UC9 ..> UC8 : <<extend>>

UC10 --> ONET
UC6 --> ONET

note bottom of UC6
  Emerging technology:
  cosine similarity over 35-dimensional
  O*NET skill-importance vectors.
  Requirements FR-06, TR-01, TR-02, TR-03.
end note
@enduml
